-- =============================================================================
-- S004: partner catalog settings (enabled specialties/insurers/medications, prices, stock)
-- SYNTHETIC DEMO DATA ONLY. Never apply to a database that holds real patients.
-- Applied by scripts/apply-seeds.sh after migrations V001+ and after the catalog DB
-- has been seeded (rxlink-catalog-db C006): catalog references use its fixed codes.
-- =============================================================================
-- What the old migrations V030/V031 derived implicitly: the partner enables catalog entries
-- and sets its own prices. Keyed by catalog code, no foreign keys (catalog is another DB).
-- Insurance coverage overrides: none (the old values equal the catalog defaults).
-- Stock: medications used by the S003 prescriptions start with 100 units / reorder level 20,
-- the rest at 0 (not counted yet) in the default clinic.




SELECT c."ClinicId", v."MedicationCode"::uuid, v."StockQuantity", v."ReorderLevel"
  FROM "Clinic" c
